   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">In my console I see the following warning which might or might not be related: <div><br></div><div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\" size=\"1\" color=\"#ff0000\">Warning message:</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\" size=\"1\" color=\"#ff0000\">In bind_rows_(x, .id) : Unequal factor levels: coercing to character</font></div></div><div><br></div><div>I found the following: </div><div><a href=\"https://stackoverflow.com/questions/30203299/bind-rows-in-dplyr-throwing-unusual-error\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://stackoverflow.com/questions/30203299/bind-rows-in-dplyr-throwing-unusual-error&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792484591071000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0jWC_tWSRSz0rKYc6x-Ss-\">https://stackoverflow.com/questions/30203299/bind-rows-in-dplyr-throwing-unusual-error</a><br></div><div><br></div><div>Which led me to this discussion between Romain and Hadley on the issue. </div><div><a href=\"https://github.com/hadley/dplyr/issues/112\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/hadley/dplyr/issues/112&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792484591071000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3nFToe3_1Oamh3sRvkxOIB\">https://github.com/hadley/dplyr/issues/112</a><br></div><div><br></div><div>I don&#39;t know the guts of ggvis well enough to comment further. Hopefully Hadley sees this and can comment. </div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
